    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Exploratory machine-learning analytics</h2>

      <p>
        PlantLife365 includes a controlled tabular regression workflow for
        research exploration. Available methods include linear regression,
        random forest regression, gradient boosting regression, support vector
        regression, and K-nearest neighbors regression. The workflow reports
        MAE, RMSE, R-squared, actual-versus-predicted diagnostics, and
        model-specific descriptive feature scores where available.
      </p>

      <p>
        These tools are intended for exploratory analysis of user-provided
        sensor data. They are not presented as a validated agronomic forecasting
        or recommendation model. This distinction keeps the platform useful for
        research while clearly separating analytical experimentation from
        verified agricultural guidance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Optional local AI assistance</h2>

      <p>
        The maintained application also supports an optional local
        Ollama-compatible assistant. When enabled, the assistant receives a
        compact context assembled from the authenticated user's current
        monitoring information and recent user-owned logs.
      </p>

      <p>
        The local design supports privacy-conscious experimentation and keeps
        monitoring context scoped to the authenticated user. Generated
        responses remain advisory interface output and are not treated as
        verified agronomic recommendations.
      </p>
    </section>

